    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d635">

                <pb facs="0603" n="437" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg437"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 837.156/226</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Minister Gonzales </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-03-24T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 24, 1916, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your March 22, 1 p.m. Department is unofficially advised that the commission to
                    study Cuban Ports matter has three months in which to report. Cable briefly your
                    opinion as to the present status of this matter, both political and otherwise
                    and whether this apparently dilatory procedure may be expected to achieve
                    results.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
